 "scope": "Fixed binary Koblitz standard-subspace bases and one K13 known-answer development target; signed independent verification and EKS performance measurement absent",
 "statement": "On the fixed K13/d5, K19/d7, and K23/d8 public Koblitz bases, the producer collision census and a separate dense row-rank replay recorded 27, 99, and 201 checked nonzero pair-sum rows with ranks 5, 11, and 23; a source-pinned ecbench development suite passed 21 tests with one ignored, including same-target K13 scalar verification under old and opt-in harvest engines. This is producer development evidence, not a verified performance or ECDLP cost claim."
